has-session exit-code parity between the cmux compat layer and real tmux

Flipping detection to true makes `killTmuxSessionIfExists` route through
`cmux __tmux-compat` for the first time. That helper reads a non-zero
`has-session` exit as "session does not exist", so an inverted convention on
the cmux side would either skip cleanup or kill the wrong target. Measured
rather than assumed:

$ /Applications/cmux.app/Contents/Resources/bin/cmux __tmux-compat has-session \
      -t omo-pr6390-does-not-exist-xyz
  Error: Workspace target not found: omo-pr6390-does-not-exist-xyz
  exit 1

$ /opt/homebrew/bin/tmux has-session -t omo-pr6390-does-not-exist-xyz
  exit 1

Both report a missing session as non-zero, so the existing guard keeps its
meaning under the compat layer. (The real-tmux invocation reports a connection
error rather than a missing session because the cmux shim's TMUX is still
exported in this shell; the exit code, which is what the guard reads, matches.)
